            <title>[LU-21181] ptlrpc: bulk descriptor too small on 64K-page servers (bd_iov_count &lt;= bd_max_iov LBUG)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21181</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;On a node with PAGE_SIZE &amp;gt; 4096 (aarch64, 64KiB pages), an OSS crashes in the bulk write path:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity test 119p (unaligned DIO writev, offsets 0x7ffff/0x100001/0x180000) on a 64K-page node. It crashes the server every time. The same test passes on a 4K-page node with the same tree.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;LustreError: (client.c:270:__ptlrpc_add_bulk_chunk()) ASSERTION( desc-&amp;gt;bd_iov_count &amp;lt;= desc-&amp;gt;bd_max_iov ) failed:
LBUG
  __ptlrpc_prep_bulk_page → ptlrpc_prep_bulk_page_nopin → tgt_brw_write → tgt_handle_request0&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cause: __ptlrpc_prep_bulk_page() splits a page into two kiovs when it crosses an LNET_MTU MD boundary (introduced with &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19180" title="interop sanityn test_16a: fsx with O_DIRECT failed." class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19180"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19180&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20520" title="Large unaligned bulk write hangs when client and server page sizes differ" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20520"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20520&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, which key MD boundaries on the 4KiB-virtual bd_iop_len). With 4K pages this never happens, so one kiov per page is enough. A 64K page can cross boundary, and ptlrpc_new_bulk() allocates bd_vec with exactly nfrags entries. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20520" title="Large unaligned bulk write hangs when client and server page sizes differ" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20520"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20520&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; noted this gap in its commit message: “A large-page server needs a separate fix: ptlrpc_prep_bulk_exp() sizes the descriptor at the bare page count, with no room for the split kiovs.”&lt;/p&gt;</description>
